"""Independent 2038/I-L solutions."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ANSWERS=[
('2038/I','For starting sport x, the winner is the lexicographically maximum row after cyclically rotating its columns to start at x: at each sport the current maximum prefix group survives. Rank every cyclic row substring by doubling. Use global rank pairs (rank[row,col],rank[row,col+len mod m]) and stable counting sorts to compute ranks of doubled lengths. Once length>=m these ranks order complete rotations; extra repeated columns cannot change their first differing bit. For each column choose the row with greatest final rank. O(n*m*log m) time and O(n*m) memory.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;int main(){ios::sync_with_stdio(false);cin.tie(nullptr);int n,m;cin>>n>>m;int N=n*m;vector<int>rank(N),next(N),order(N),tmp(N),second(N),cnt(max(N+2,4));for(int i=0;i<n;i++){string s;cin>>s;for(int j=0;j<m;j++)rank[i*m+j]=s[j]-'0';}int classes=2;for(int len=1;len<m;len*=2){for(int i=0;i<N;i++)second[i]=(i/m)*m+(i%m+len)%m;iota(order.begin(),order.end(),0);auto counting=[&](bool other){fill(cnt.begin(),cnt.begin()+classes,0);for(int x:order)cnt[rank[other?second[x]:x]]++;int sum=0;for(int k=0;k<classes;k++){int v=cnt[k];cnt[k]=sum;sum+=v;}for(int x:order)tmp[cnt[rank[other?second[x]:x]]++]=x;order.swap(tmp);};counting(true);counting(false);int nc=0;for(int t=0;t<N;t++){int x=order[t];if(t&& (rank[x]!=rank[order[t-1]]||rank[second[x]]!=rank[second[order[t-1]]]))nc++;next[x]=nc;}classes=nc+1;rank.swap(next);}for(int j=0;j<m;j++){int best=0;for(int i=1;i<n;i++)if(rank[i*m+j]>rank[best*m+j])best=i;cout<<best+1<<(j+1==m?'\n':' ');}}'''),
('2038/J','Track the number waiting excluding Monocarp, assuming he declines every earlier bus. A bus is available iff its capacity strictly exceeds this number; afterwards reduce the waiting count by its capacity, floored at zero. Since he may decline earlier buses this gives feasibility independently for each bus. O(n) time, O(1) space.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;int main(){int n;cin>>n;long long waiting=0;while(n--){char c;long long x;cin>>c>>x;if(c=='P')waiting+=x;else{cout<<(x>waiting?"YES":"NO")<<'\n';waiting=max(0LL,waiting-x);}}}'''),
('2038/K','Let r be the last row <=n coprime to a and c the last column <=n coprime to b. A path reaching (r,c) can attain the lower bound sum(i=1..r)gcd(i,a)+sum(j=1..c)gcd(j,b)+(r+c-2), by using row 1 for horizontal moves and column c for vertical moves. Earlier repeated row/column costs are at least one. Any moves beyond r or c that occur before the other coordinate reaches c or r can be postponed to pass through (r,c) without increasing cost, because both gcd values there are one. Then ordinary grid DP only on the short tail rectangle [r,n]*[c,n] is sufficient. O(n log(max(a,b))+(n-r+1)*(n-c+1)) time and O(n-c+1) memory.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;using ll=long long;int main(){int n,a,b;cin>>n>>a>>b;int r=n,c=n;while(__gcd(r,a)!=1)--r;while(__gcd(c,b)!=1)--c;ll base=r+c-2;for(int i=1;i<=r;i++)base+=__gcd(i,a);for(int j=1;j<=c;j++)base+=__gcd(j,b);const ll INF=1LL<<60;vector<ll>dp(n-c+1,INF);for(int i=r;i<=n;i++)for(int j=c;j<=n;j++){int k=j-c;if(i==r&&j==c){dp[k]=base;continue;}ll cost=__gcd(i,a)+__gcd(j,b),best=dp[k];if(k)best=min(best,dp[k-1]);dp[k]=best+cost;}cout<<dp.back()<<'\n';}'''),
('2038/L','Assign weights 1/3 to each 18 and 21 piece and 1/2 to each 25 piece. Every feasible cutting pattern has weight <=1 (three small pieces fit, two 25s fit, but a 25 plus two small pieces do not). Hence at least ceil(7n/6) planks are needed. Six sets of demands can be packed in seven planks: three patterns (25,25), three (18,21,21), one (18,18,18). For residues n=0..5 the optimum is respectively 0,2,3,4,5,6, attainable by direct small patterns. Thus ceil(7n/6) is tight. O(1) time and memory.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;int main(){int n;cin>>n;cout<<(7*n+5)/6<<'\n';}''')]
if __name__=='__main__':
    p=Path('backend/data/bench/codeforces700_20261116/assistant_answers_v1/shard_test_000_199.jsonl')
    with p.open('a',encoding='utf-8') as out:
        for ident,explanation,code in ANSWERS:
            out.write(json.dumps({'id':ident,'split':'test','author':'current chat assistant','status':'authored','explanation':explanation,'cpp_code':code,'validation':'not executed'})+'\n')
